# The build context is the repository root (docker build -f apps/api/Dockerfile .). Nothing is
# sent unless it is listed here, so that neither a private signing key nor a local .env nor
# node_modules can end up in an image or on a remote builder.
# The same list is in Dockerfile.dockerignore (BuildKit reads that name next to the Dockerfile);
# a test keeps the two files identical.

*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!.npmrc
!tsconfig.base.json

!apps/api
!apps/mobile/package.json
!apps/mobile/assets/packs
!packages/shared
!packages/content-tools

# Public keys only (content/keys also holds the private development key, which is git-ignored).
!content/keys/*.pub

# Whatever the folders above contain locally:
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/coverage
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/*.key
